#: includes/pages/settings.php:187
msgid "Choose whether Preview or Editor mode opens first in both the Metadata and Media Attributes editors. You can switch modes at any time inside an editor."
msgstr "Kies of de modus Preview of Editor als eerste wordt geopend in zowel de Metadata- als de Media Attributes-editors. Je kunt binnen een editor op elk moment van modus wisselen."

#: includes/pages/settings.php:176
msgid "Default editor mode:"
msgstr "Standaard editormodus:"

#: includes/pages/help.php:1028
msgid "How do I switch between Preview and Editor mode in the Metadata or Media Attributes editor?"
msgstr "Hoe wissel ik tussen de modi Preview en Editor in de Metadata- of Media Attributes-editor?"

#: includes/pages/help.php:1027
msgid "Use the Preview and Editor buttons at the top of either editor. Preview shows estimated appearances and field-specific guidance, while Editor shows the existing inputs and generation controls. Choose the normal opening mode under Settings > General > Default editor mode. Existing installations upgraded from 2.4.3 or earlier begin in Editor mode unless a mode was already stored."
msgstr "Gebruik de knoppen Preview en Editor bovenaan beide editors. Preview toont geschatte weergaven en veldspecifieke begeleiding, terwijl Editor de bestaande invoer en generatieknoppen toont. Kies de normale openingsmodus onder Settings > General > Default editor mode. Bestaande installaties die zijn geüpgraded vanaf 2.4.3 of ouder starten in Editor-modus, tenzij er al een modus was opgeslagen."

#: includes/pages/help.php:813
msgid "<b>Media attribute editor</b>: Use Preview mode to inspect WordPress-style Title and Description presentations, Alt Text accessibility output, and a theme-neutral Caption example with guidance. Use Editor mode to change or generate the existing media attribute fields. Custom Instructions and Generate All remain available in either workflow."
msgstr "<b>Media attribute editor</b>: gebruik de modus Preview om WordPress-achtige presentaties van Title en Description, Alt Text-uitvoer voor toegankelijkheid en een themaneutraal Caption-voorbeeld met begeleiding te bekijken. Gebruik de modus Editor om bestaande media attribute-velden te wijzigen of te genereren. Custom Instructions en Generate All blijven in beide workflows beschikbaar."

#: includes/pages/help.php:810
msgid "<b>Metadata editor</b>: Use Preview mode to review approximate Google, Facebook, X, WhatsApp, and keyword appearances together with field-specific guidance. Use Editor mode to change the existing inputs or generate individual fields. Focus Keyphrase and Custom Instructions remain prominent generation context, and Generate All stays available in the compact editor header. Choose the normal opening mode under Settings -> General -> Default editor mode."
msgstr "<b>Metadata editor</b>: gebruik de modus Preview om benaderende Google-, Facebook-, X-, WhatsApp- en keyword-weergaven samen met veldspecifieke begeleiding te bekijken. Gebruik de modus Editor om bestaande invoer te wijzigen of afzonderlijke velden te genereren. Focus Keyphrase en Custom Instructions blijven prominente generatiecontext, en Generate All blijft beschikbaar in de compacte editorheader. Kies de normale openingsmodus onder Settings -> General -> Default editor mode."

